## Google's trademarks and material

Google, Google Cloud, Gemini, Vertex AI and the other Google product names used here are trademarks
of Google LLC. This project is independent: it is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by
Google, and it uses those names only to say which exam and products it is about.

The Google Cloud logo on the home page (`quiz/components/atoms/google-cloud-logo.tsx`) is Google's
trademark. It is drawn from a Wikimedia Commons copy of Google's artwork, with the cloud in Google's
colours and the wordmark in the page's text colour, to name the exam the app prepares for. It does
not imply any relationship with Google, and it is not covered by the MIT licence.

Google's exam guide, study guide and product documentation are cited and linked from `glossary.md`
and `exam-sections.md`; they are not included here. Many glossary meanings are short summaries of
Google's study guide and documentation, each with its source; Google keeps all rights in its own
text, and this licence does not cover it.

The online demo, published on GitHub Pages, serves the same app: the same Google Cloud logo and
glossary text, under the same terms as above. It stores nothing on a server.

Read Aloud (`quiz/app/read`) fetches the learning path's course text live from Google's public
course bundle, and caches spoken clips of it on the machine that runs the quiz. That text is
Google's and is not included here. Whoever runs the quiz fetches it, for their own study, and is
responsible for following Google's terms for it.

## Voices

The spoken voice comes from the macOS text-to-speech voice of the machine that runs the quiz, under
Apple's terms for that machine. No voice or audio is included in this repository.
